---
title: Patio Chicken
author: Mildred McKinzie
category: Meat, Poultry, Fish
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@chicken{1%cut up}
@flour{1/2%c}
@butter{1/2%c}
@sliced fresh mushrooms{1/2%lb}
@milk{1/2%c}
@salt and pepper
@sour cream{2%c}

Dip chicken pieces in milk and roll in flour seasoned with salt and pepper. Melt butter in skillet and brown chicken pieces. Place chicken pieces in a casserole. Saute mushrooms in the butter for about 5 minutes. Spoon over chicken pieces. Cover mushrooms and chicken with sour cream. Bake in a slow oven (325 degrees) 30 to 45 minutes or until chicken is tender.
